// The goal gate's state: what has been commanded, what is queued for later,
// and when the commander was last heard from.
//
// This is the driver's own cross-cycle memory, and it is a schema because every
// host of the gate keeps it somewhere a process restart or a slot crossing can
// read: the simulated driver keeps it in its state slot, and the motor driver
// process keeps the same declaration in its own memory. One description, so the
// two cannot disagree about which goal is due or about how long silence has
// gone on.
//
// Its own module, apart from the setpoint it queues, because a gate is state
// and a setpoint is a message: whoever only commands the machine must not
// rebuild when the gate grows a field.
//
// Time is `SyncTime`, never a bare nanosecond count. A queue's length is the
// array's own, so no separate number can disagree with it.

#![generate(cpp)]
#![cpp(namespace=brenn_reachy::driver)]

use driver::goal;

// A goal queue, the setpoint being held, and the dead-man's last observation.
//
// A slot nothing wrote reads as a gate that has been told nothing: an empty
// queue, nothing held, no latch, and a dead-man that is not running -- which is
// what a driver nobody has spoken to yet is, rather than a driver that has gone
// quiet.
schema GateState
{
    uuid: 4d0c6f2a-9b3e-4a51-8f6d-2c7a1e5b04d9;
    fields
    {
        // Goals accepted and not yet executed, oldest first. One executes per
        // cycle, so a burst drains at the cycle rate rather than becoming a
        // jump; a goal offered to a full queue is refused rather than absorbed.
        #0 queue: VarArray<goal::GoalSetpoint, 5>;

        // The setpoint currently held, rewritten every cycle no new goal is due
        // for -- what keeps a servo's position loop awake between goals.
        // Meaningful only when `has_held`.
        #1 held: goal::GoalSetpoint;

        // Whether anything has ever been commanded.
        #2 has_held: Bool;

        // Whether the gate has latched torque off. Only a fresh arming ends a
        // latch, and while it stands the gate asks for a torque-off sweep every
        // cycle.
        #3 latched: Bool;

        // When liveness was last observed -- an accepted goal, or an arming.
        // Meaningful only when `has_accepted`.
        #4 last_accept: SyncTime;

        // Whether liveness has ever been observed. Until it has, the dead-man
        // does not run.
        #5 has_accepted: Bool;
    }
}
